# anonfm_vsrat_reader colour scheme.
#
# Copy this file to one of (the reader picks the first one that exists):
#   ./anonfm_colors.conf
#   $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/anonfm/colors.conf
#   ~/.config/anonfm/colors.conf
#   %APPDATA%\anonfm\colors.conf            (Windows)
# Or pass it explicitly with --colors PATH.
#
# Format:
#   <kind> <nick> <color>
#
# kind:    listener       — colour of the listener nick badge
#          dj             — colour of the DJ nick badge
#          listener_text  — colour of the listener message body
#          dj_text        — colour of the DJ response body
#
# nick:    exact match against the JSON field, OR '*' for the category default.
#
# color:   xterm-256 colour index 0..255,
#          OR `hash` — pick from the built-in palette by FNV-1a(nick),
#          OR `off`  — do not colour.
#
# Defaults if no rule matches:
#   badges:  `hash`  (each nick gets a stable palette colour)
#   bodies:  252     (one consistent soft-grey for ALL bodies — the badge
#                     identifies who, the body conveys what; matching the
#                     body to the speaker's badge colour just makes the
#                     screen noisy without adding info)
# Set `*_text  *  off` if you want naked monochrome bodies, or pick any
# xterm-256 index / `hash` to opt back into per-nick body colouring.
#
# Comments start with '#'. Blank lines OK.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Category defaults
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
listener        *  hash
dj              *  hash

listener_text   *  252       # one stable colour for all listener bodies
dj_text         *  252       # ditto for DJs — keep the eye anchored
# listener_text *  hash      # opt-in: each listener's body in their badge colour
# listener_text *  off       # opt-in: monochrome bodies

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DJ roster — pin specific colours so they stay constant across machines
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# We have ~1.5 active DJs at any given moment. The DJ palette is small
# on purpose (3 cycle colours), so pinning here is more about taste than
# collision-avoidance.
#
# Uncomment / edit to taste. Standard recognisable assignments:
#
# dj            Kriesh        226    # bright yellow
# dj            Obsidian      118    # bright green
# dj            <kто-там-ещё> 214    # orange — third seat when manned
#
# dj_text       Kriesh        226    # match body to badge for full presence
# dj_text       Obsidian      118

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listener regulars — pin nicks of frequent flyers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is just a hint list. Add your own usual suspects here so the
# colour stays the same even if the hash palette is tweaked later.
#
# listener      araaerkb08ba    96
# listener      <regular_nick>  117
# listener      <another_one>   207
#
# listener_text araaerkb08ba    96   # mirror the badge colour into the body
